Show the drop shadow size the dialog was given

QtCurveConfig::setWidgetOptions() reads the process wide
qtcX11ShadowSize() for the drop shadow size. Every neighbouring line
reads the options that the caller gave. The Defaults button therefore
keeps the size of the current configuration. A return to the current
preset shows the size of the preset that the user opened last. The
next Apply writes that stale size over the saved one.

Read opts.shadowSize, the way the line above it reads
opts.menuBgndOpacity. Both qtcDefaultSettings() and qtcReadConfig()
put the wanted size in the options, so the dialog must show it.

The change sits on the branch work/dialog-state of the local tree, as commit 2 of 12.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

diff --git a/qt6/config/qtcurveconfig.cpp b/qt6/config/qtcurveconfig.cpp
index 55e76bed..f07ae914 100644
--- a/qt6/config/qtcurveconfig.cpp
+++ b/qt6/config/qtcurveconfig.cpp
@@ -3545,7 +3545,7 @@ void QtCurveConfig::setWidgetOptions(const Options &opts)
     dlgOpacity->setValue(opts.dlgOpacity);
     menuBgndImage->setCurrentIndex(opts.menuBgndImage.type);
     menuBgndOpacity->setValue(opts.menuBgndOpacity);
-    dropShadowSize->setValue(qtcX11ShadowSize());
+    dropShadowSize->setValue(opts.shadowSize);
     dwtAppearance->setCurrentIndex(opts.dwtAppearance);
     tooltipAppearance->setCurrentIndex(opts.tooltipAppearance);
     dwtBtnAsPerTitleBar->setChecked(opts.dwtSettings&DWT_BUTTONS_AS_PER_TITLEBAR);
